    "title": "Brookwood girls wrap up No. 1 spot in 7- with sweep of Norcross - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By From Staff Reports ,\n6 hours ago Scenes from Norcross at Brookwood girls basketball in Snellville, GA on February 4, 2026. By JAMIE SPAAR SNELLVILLE — Brookwood wrapped up the No. 1 spot in Region 7- girls basketball for the regular season on Wednesday.\nThe host Broncos completed a sweep of Norcross in the regular season with a 53-46 win that boosted their 7- lead to two games over second-place Norcross (16-6, 10-2) with two games left in the regular season. Brookwood (17-6, 12-0) beat Norcross 34-29 in the teams’ first meeting on January 6.\nNorcross has a two-game lead over third-place North Gwinnett (8-4 region).\nTaylor Liberal had 19 points, nine rebounds and four steals, and Justyce McCoy had 17 points, five rebounds and four steals to lead the Brookwood victory. Mya Wilson added 10 points and three rebounds.",
